deep.reconstruction:
Setting (from the surrounding pages of 'variations sur l'équation des lacets'). 𝔊 is a profinite group with distinguished elements ρ, σ, τ, τ'. The 'universal case' that opens the next page is 𝔊 = GL(2,ℤ)^, with ρ of order 6, σ of order 4, and τ, τ' reflections, so the pair (ρ,σ) is modelled on the generators of SL(2,ℤ) and on the genus-1 situation. 𝔊^+ is the 'orientation-preserving' index-2 part. L_ρ and L_σ are the procyclic subgroups generated by ρ and σ.

Attached to (𝔊,ρ,σ) Grothendieck has built a tower of objects:
- Σ_{ρ,σ}^𝔊, a set of 'solutions' with an 'étale' subset Σ^{ét};
- Z_{ρ,σ}^𝔊, a group of automorphisms u of 𝔊^+ that normalize L_σ and send L_ρ, L_σ to 𝔊^+-conjugates of themselves, with maps γ, ε_Z, ε'_Z;
- G_{ρ,σ} = Z·𝔊^+, together with normalizers N_ρ, N_σ and their subgroups N_ρ^*, N_σ^*;
- groups S_0 M_{ρ,σ} and M_{ρ,σ}, assembled from these pieces via maps Θ_Z, Θ_ρ, Θ_σ, Θ_G and diagrams (45), (62).
These are Grothendieck–Teichmüller / Out-type symmetry groups of the 'loop equation' for this triangle-group-like datum.

The section '7° Fonctorialités' (previous page and this one) asks how this construction behaves under a surjection φ: 𝔊 → 𝔊' of profinite groups, with ρ, σ, τ pushed forward.
- The Proposition gives equivalent conditions on φ:
  (a) the induced map Σ^𝔊 → Σ^{𝔊'} preserves the étale parts;
  (b), (b') every relevant u ∈ Aut 𝔊^+ descends to some u' ∈ Aut 𝔊'^+, i.e. u normalizes Ker φ;
  (c) there is a homomorphism φ_Z: Z^𝔊 → Z^{𝔊'} compatible with γ, ε_Z, ε'_Z and with the descent square (90);
  (c') there is a homomorphism φ_G: G^𝔊 → G^{𝔊'} with the same properties.
- This page finishes (c'): φ_G is unique and compatible with i_{𝔊,G} and i_{Z,G}. It sends N_ρ^𝔊 into N_ρ^{𝔊'} and N_σ^𝔊 into N_σ^{𝔊'}, extending to φ_ρ, φ_σ that induce maps on the starred subgroups N^*.
- Such φ is called 'prolongeable'.
- Corollary: φ then extends to φ_M: S_0 M^𝔊 → S_0 M^{𝔊'}. This is compatible with Θ_Z, Θ_ρ, Θ_σ, Θ_G (given φ_Z, φ_ρ, φ_σ, φ_G) and with the diagrams (45), (62). So the M-construction is a functor on the category of prolongeable quotients.
- Example: if Σ^{𝔊'} = Σ^{𝔊' ét} (everything in the target is étale), condition (a) holds trivially, so every surjection onto such a 𝔊' is prolongeable.
- Remark: one may instead fix a subgroup Z^♮ ⊂ Z^𝔊 and require the descent condition only for u ∈ Z^♮. From Z^♮ one builds:
  - G^♮ = Z^♮·𝔊^+;
  - Z_ρ^♮ = Z_ρ ∩ G^♮ and Z_σ^♮ = Z_σ ∩ G^♮;
  - hence N_ρ^♮, N_ρ^{♮*}, N_σ^♮, N_σ^{♮*}, γ^♮;
  - and finally S_0 M^♮ and M^♮.
  An obvious variant of the Proposition then gives conditions for extending φ to S_0 M^♮ → S_0 M^{𝔊'}. A marginal note adds that one must then also assume c_Z ∈ Z^*_{ρ,σ}.
- The point: functoriality of these GT-type groups along quotients. One passes from the universal profinite case GL(2,ℤ)^ to its quotients, in effect finite or characteristic quotients and dessins-type data, compatibly with all the structure maps.
